const TREASURE17_ART={"quay-ground": {"asset": "assets/treasure17/quay-ground.80d04fb57059.webp", "size": [1536, 1024], "alpha": false}, "garden-ground": {"asset": "assets/treasure17/garden-ground.de3bc7325bef.webp", "size": [1536, 1024], "alpha": false}, "footbridge": {"asset": "assets/treasure17/footbridge.d3f62f635df2.webp", "size": [1024, 1536], "alpha": true}, "garden-key": {"asset": "assets/treasure17/garden-key.3421300a5738.webp", "size": [1536, 1024], "alpha": true}};
const TREASURE17_BOOKS={"bond": {"title": "The Bell Before the Bargain", "pages": ["Before the first boat arrived, the King’s Son went down into the creditor’s prison. He did not bargain with its keeper for a smaller cruelty. He bore the bond and broke its claim. The quay bell rang over an open door.", "Harven heard the bell. Yet each morning he unfolded the old slate. The whisper knew his broken promises, his sharp words, his failures at the bench. It fastened a new price to each remembered wrong.", "Maerin brought the cancelled bond. “Some accusations tell the truth about a wound,” she said. “They do not tell the truth about the Son. His payment is not a beginning you must finish.”", "Harven took down the toll slate. Then he went to the boatyard to return timber he had borrowed. The work had not become unnecessary. It had become the work of a free man.", "The allegory points to Christ’s forgiveness and victory in Colossians 2:13–15, and grace leading to good works in Ephesians 2:8–10. Scripture speaks of Christ himself. Finding seals or recalling words does not buy his gift."]}, "garden": {"title": "The Key and the Common Trough", "pages": ["The Son’s messengers brought Neris three little seeds, freely, before she had a garden. She had wanted to present them with a great harvest. They had asked instead whether she would receive them.", "Rook admired the garden. He wanted its door always open to him. “If you trusted me,” he said, “you would put the key in my keeping.” Neris would offer a meal, a task, a chair. The key remained hers.", "One day the key fell by the arch. A traveler found it. The path offered no thunder, no painted warning. Only a small choice: give back what belonged to another, or use it to buy a place with the loudest voice.", "They returned the key, then worked together. Neris held the intake. Rook carried buckets. The traveler turned the wheels. Water moved through the beds and onward to the common trough; no one had to possess the spring to share its gift.", "The trail joins 1 John 4:19 with Galatians 5:13: God’s love comes first, and freedom serves through love. A garden key illustrates a person’s agency; it is not a claim that people must earn love or surrender their boundaries."]}};
const TREASURE17_SCRIPTURE_MD="# Treasure trail readings · KJV\n\nSeparate lesson readings. These do not replace or enlarge the original 84-card discovery deck. The prose around them is original fiction; the passages are Scripture. Read the full passage before recalling its headline. KJV wording, references and verse boundaries are retained.\n\n## Colossians 2:13–15 (KJV)\n\n### Blotting out the handwriting of ordinances that was against us\n\n[2:13] And you, being dead in your sins and the uncircumcision of your flesh, hath he quickened together with him, having forgiven you all trespasses;\n[2:14] Blotting out the handwriting of ordinances that was against us, which was contrary to us, and took it out of the way, nailing it to his cross;\n[2:15] And having spoiled principalities and powers, he made a shew of them openly, triumphing over them in it.\n\n*Tags: Christ, cross, forgiveness, victory*\n\n#### Metadata\n```json\n{\"id\":\"treasure-cancelled-bond\",\"translation\":\"KJV\",\"lesson\":\"bond\"}\n```\n\n## Ephesians 2:8–10 (KJV)\n\n### For by grace are ye saved through faith\n\n[2:8] For by grace are ye saved through faith; and that not of yourselves: it is the gift of God:\n[2:9] Not of works, lest any man should boast.\n[2:10] For we are his workmanship, created in Christ Jesus unto good works, which God hath before ordained that we should walk in them.\n\n*Tags: grace, faith, Christ, gift, good works*\n\n#### Metadata\n```json\n{\"id\":\"treasure-gift-before-work\",\"translation\":\"KJV\",\"lesson\":\"bond\"}\n```\n\n## 1 John 4:19 (KJV)\n\n### We love him, because he first loved us.\n\n[4:19] We love him, because he first loved us.\n\n*Tags: love, received love, God*\n\n#### Metadata\n```json\n{\"id\":\"treasure-loved-first\",\"translation\":\"KJV\",\"lesson\":\"garden\"}\n```\n\n## Galatians 5:13 (KJV)\n\n### by love serve one another.\n\n[5:13] For, brethren, ye have been called unto liberty; only use not liberty for an occasion to the flesh, but by love serve one another.\n\n*Tags: Christ, freedom, love, service*\n\n#### Metadata\n```json\n{\"id\":\"treasure-free-to-serve\",\"translation\":\"KJV\",\"lesson\":\"garden\"}\n```\n";
